const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"检验方法会不会自己制造事件",en:"Can the test manufacture an event?"},body:{zh:"Brown与Warner研究日收益的厚尾、非同步交易与方差变化，是否会破坏事件研究中的统计检验。问题是方法在没有异常表现时会不会误报，以及存在给定异常表现时能不能发现，而不是证明某一类公司公告必然影响价格。",en:"Brown and Warner ask how daily-return properties affect event-study tests. They examine false rejection when abnormal performance is absent and detection when a known effect is introduced. They do not establish the impact of one particular announcement category."}},{title:{zh:"真实收益配上虚构事件日",en:"Actual returns, artificial event dates"},body:{zh:"作者从CRSP随机有放回抽取证券与事件日期，构造250组、每组50只证券，日期范围为1962年7月至1979年12月。收益来自历史市场，但事件是随机指定的。因此这是一项方法模拟，不能把样本理解成250次真实公告。",en:"The experiment constructs 250 samples of 50 securities, drawing securities and event dates with replacement from CRSP, July 1962–December 1979. Returns are historical, but events are assigned randomly. These are methodological simulations, not 250 observed announcement episodes."},reference:{url:"https://bandi.feb.uns.ac.id/wp-content/uploads/2010/03/brown-warner-1985-1.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第3.1节：实验样本",en:"Original §3.1: experimental samples"}}},{title:{zh:"先估计正常表现，再看事件窗口",en:"Estimate normal performance first"},body:{zh:"每只证券最多使用事件前244日至后5日的250个日收益；前239日为估计期，最后11日为事件期。作者比较均值调整、市场调整和OLS市场模型。不同基准给出不同的异常收益定义，估计窗口与事件窗口不能互相污染。",en:"Up to 250 returns span days −244 through +5: 239 estimation days and an 11-day event period. Mean-adjusted, market-adjusted and OLS market-model measures are compared. Each benchmark defines abnormal performance differently, and estimation and event windows must remain separate."},reference:{url:"https://bandi.feb.uns.ac.id/wp-content/uploads/2010/03/brown-warner-1985-1.pdf",label:{zh:"原文第3.1–3.2节：窗口与超额收益",en:"Original §§3.1–3.2: windows and excess returns"}}},{title:{zh:"误报率和检验能力是两件事",en:"Size and power are different"},body:{zh:"没有人为加入异常收益时，观察拒绝原假设的频率；随后向事件日收益加入已知幅度，观察方法能否检出。前者考察误报，后者考察检验能力。仅展示一次显著结果，既不能证明方法校准，也不能说明未显著时确实没有经济效应。",en:"With no added abnormal return, rejection frequency measures test size. Adding a known event-day effect probes power. One significant result establishes neither calibration nor the ability to detect plausible effects; an insignificant result is not automatically evidence of no economic effect."}},{title:{zh:"结果不是忽略相关性的通行证",en:"The findings are not a dependence waiver"},body:{zh:"论文报告标准日频方法在不少模拟情形下表现良好，同时指出超额收益自相关和事件引起的方差变化有时值得调整。某些设定中更复杂的相关性处理未必更有检验力，但不能据此忽略真实样本中的集中事件、共同冲击或重叠窗口。",en:"Standard daily procedures perform well in many simulations, while serial dependence and event-induced variance changes sometimes warrant adjustment. More elaborate dependence correction need not always improve power, but that is not permission to ignore clustered events, common shocks or overlapping windows."}},{title:{zh:"从事件定义开始落地",en:"Begin with an event definition"},body:{zh:"编辑建议：先确定事件身份、可得时间与交易日映射，再定义估计窗口、基准和样本单位。对集中发生的事件单独检查依赖结构，并保留未对齐记录。本板块的事件时间线教程只完成这些准备，不替代异常收益估计或因果识别。",en:"Editorial application: define event identity, availability and session mapping before choosing windows, benchmarks and sampling units. Inspect dependence for clustered events and retain unresolved records. The event-timeline tutorial handles preparation only, not abnormal-return estimation or causal identification."}}],readerLimits:{zh:"随机事件模拟的良好表现不自动适用于集中公告、选择性事件或另一市场的交易制度。",en:"Performance under random-event simulation does not automatically transfer to clustered announcements, selected events or another market's trading institutions."}};export{e as default};
